[center]
[size=6][color=#74C7F5][b]BODY CHANGE NG[/b][/color][/size]
[size=4][color=#B7DDF2]Change BodySlide presets, actor skins, and player tint masks in real time[/color][/size]

[color=#9AD7F5][b]NATIVE IN-GAME GUI  •  GAMEPAD SUPPORT  •  LIVE NPC DISTRIBUTION[/b][/color]
[/center]

[line]

[size=5][color=#5FB8E8][b]OVERVIEW[/b][/color][/size]

Body Change NG manages BodySlide body morphs, actor skin textures, and player RaceMenu tint layers from one native in-game interface. Select the player or a loaded NPC, preview changes immediately, edit NPC distribution conditions in game, and either distribute to loaded NPCs now or save the rules for the next launch.

[b]No MCM. No manual distribution-JSON editing. No runtime body-mesh replacement.[/b]

[line]

[size=5][color=#5FB8E8][b]WHY BODY CHANGE NG?[/b][/color][/size]

[size=4][color=#9AD7F5][b]Compared with OBody NG[/b][/color][/size]

Both mods ultimately deform a built body through RaceMenu BodyMorph and TRI data. Body Change NG does not swap in a separate body mesh. The difference is the selection, distribution, and state-management layer built above that shared morph pipeline.

[list]
[*][b]Native GUI instead of an MCM[/b] — press F7 to manage loaded actors, bodies, skins, player tint, and distribution rules in one scalable window
[*][b]Actor-matched Body and Skin lists[/b] — mixed CBBE 3BA and UBE installations are detected per actor from the live winning skin/head path. Skin packs additionally match the actor's humanoid, Argonian, or Khajiit race and female/male sex, so incompatible assets are not mixed; uncertain body-family evidence keeps the safe fallback visible
[*][b]Explicit rule pools[/b] — choose exactly which body presets and skin packs each rule may distribute instead of treating every installed preset as a candidate
[*][b]Independent Body and Skin decisions[/b] — distribute or exclude either category while the other category continues to use its selected pool
[*][b]Visible top-down priority[/b] — the first matching rule owns both decisions, making broad-to-specific ordering easy to inspect and edit
[*][b]Apply now or next launch[/b] — reevaluate loaded NPCs immediately, or save edits for the next launch without changing the active rules in the current session
[*][b]Save-specific results[/b] — selected results and application signatures are stored in the SKSE co-save so unchanged actors do not require full redistribution on every load
[*][b]Isolated live preview[/b] — preview, committed body, and outfit correction use separate owned morph keys; an older queued preview cannot overwrite the latest selection
[*][b]One integrated workflow[/b] — actor skins, player tint detail, RaceMenu rebuild recovery, favorites, and NPC distribution share the same UI and state model
[/list]

[size=4][color=#9AD7F5][b]Compared with Legacy Mesh-Slot Systems[/b][/color][/size]

Legacy mesh-slot systems build a separate body mesh for each predefined slot, then use Papyrus to replace prepared ESP Skin Armor, HeadPart, and TextureSet records as a unit. A skin slot therefore also requires its matching built mesh and records.

Body Change NG instead uses a native SKSE architecture without predefined ESP body slots.

[list]
[*][b]Skin is independent of mesh sets[/b] — the actor keeps its existing Skin Armor, HeadPart, and NIFs while supported texture channels are changed on the loaded body, hands, feet, and face through RaceMenu/NiOverride
[*][b]Body and Skin are freely composable[/b] — body shape is a BodyMorph preset and skin is a separate texture override; either can change without forcing a matching copy of the other
[*][b]No fixed CustomSet1-CustomSet20 slots[/b] — catalogs are built from installed BodySlide XML files and skin/tint folders
[*][b]Runtime installation and refresh[/b] — add BodySlide XML or skin/tint folders while Skyrim is running, press Refresh on that tab, and use them without rebuilding an ESP slot or restarting the game
[*][b]Player and NPC support[/b] — direct selection, conditional NPC Body/Skin distribution, and save-specific evaluated results share one implementation
[*][b]Direct tint editing[/b] — choose player tint assets, edit each layer's color and opacity immediately, or restore its captured RaceMenu value
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][color=#5FB8E8][b]FEATURES[/b][/color][/size]

[size=4][color=#9AD7F5][b]Body[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*]Select the player or a loaded NPC and apply compatible BodySlide presets immediately
[*]Low/high-weight values are interpolated using the actor's current weight
[*]Conservative BodyFamily detection keeps the main list relevant without blocking uncertain presets or filtering NPC distribution pools
[*]CBBE 3BA and UBE use the same SliderPresets folder; Preset set and Group metadata inside each XML identify its family
[*]Body application uses RaceMenu BodyMorph; no body mesh is generated or replaced while the game is running
[/list]

[size=4][color=#9AD7F5][b]Skin[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*]Apply independent skin packs to the player or a selected loaded NPC
[*]Persistent RaceMenu/NiOverride keys support body, hands, feet, face, vampire face, diffuse, normal, subsurface, specular, and compatible detail textures
[*]Partial skin packs are supported: only supplied parts and channels change, missing values retain the actor's underlying textures, and files are never substituted across body, hands, feet, or face
[*]UBE 2.0 Body/Head d-n-sk atlases are detected separately and applied to the live slot-53 body and face; known-incompatible conventional and UBE skins are never shown or distributed to the wrong detected family
[*]Argonian and Khajiit female/male folders are detected separately and matched to each actor's race and sex for preview, reapply, and NPC distribution; their body atlas is also applied to the matching live tail geometry
[*]Ownership-aware cleanup does not delete another mod's texture keys
[/list]

[size=4][color=#9AD7F5][b]Player Tint[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*]Install multiple tint packs and choose a pack from the Tint tab
[*]Automatically select a usable DDS for each layer and the player's current race
[*]Adjust color and opacity per layer immediately in game
[*]Restore the exact RaceMenu value captured before Body Change NG first changed that layer
[*]Reapply the confirmed tint selection after RaceMenu rebuilds the player
[/list]

[size=4][color=#9AD7F5][b]NPC Distribution[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*]Rules are evaluated from top to bottom; the first matching rule owns Body and Skin
[*]Body and Skin can independently distribute selected entries, be excluded from distribution, or be left unchanged
[*]Targets include all NPCs, custom followers, elders, plugins, races, factions, keywords, classes, combat styles, names, and exact NPC base FormIDs
[*]One selected preset or skin pack is fixed; multiple choices produce stable per-NPC random results
[*]Edit every condition and pool in game, then distribute to loaded NPCs immediately or save the edits for the next launch
[*]Evaluated actor results are kept in the SKSE co-save to avoid redistributing unchanged NPCs
[/list]

[b]Rules file[/b]
[b]Data\SKSE\Plugins\BodyChangeNGdistribution.json[/b]

The in-game editor writes this file, so manual JSON editing is not required. To preserve your rules when reinstalling the mod, Skyrim, or an MO2 profile, back up the file, copy it back to the same path, and press [b]Load saved values[/b] in the NPC Distribution window.

[size=4][color=#9AD7F5][b]Outfit Correction and Randomization[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*]Optional breast correction while clothed
[*]Separate nipple-correction toggle
[*]Optional stable nipple and genital slider randomization
[/list]

[size=4][color=#9AD7F5][b]UI and Input[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*]Korean, English, and Simplified Chinese UI
[*]Default F7 menu hotkey can be rebound in Mod Settings, including Ctrl, Shift, and Ctrl+Shift combinations
[*]Mouse, keyboard arrows/WASD, and gamepad D-pad navigation
[*]Gamepad confirm and cancel actions
[*]Native IME text input, Backspace, search fields, favorites, and favorites-only filtering
[/list]

[line]

