[/list]

[line]

[size=5][color=#5FB8E8][b]INSTALLATION[/b][/color][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Install the main archive with MO2
[*]Keep the included folder structure intact and enable the mod
[*]Launch Skyrim through SKSE and press F7
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][color=#5FB8E8][b]ADDING BODY PRESETS, SKIN PACKS, AND TINT PACKS[/b][/color][/size]

All paths below are relative to an MO2 mod root. You may place these assets inside Body Change NG or in separate enabled MO2 mods that provide the same virtual paths.

[size=4][color=#9AD7F5][b]Body Preset XML[/b][/color][/size]
[b]CalienteTools\BodySlide\SliderPresets\*.xml[/b]

Place standard BodySlide preset XML files in this folder.

[size=4][color=#9AD7F5][b]Skin Packs[/b][/color][/size]
[b]Conventional:[/b] BodySkin\YourSkinPack\Textures\actors\character\...
[b]CBBE 3BA female genital/anal atlas:[/b] femalebody_etc_v2_1.dds plus _msn, _sk, and _s in the conventional female directory. These files target the matching 3BA/3BBB vagina and anus geometries that share the atlas, never another body part.
[b]BHUNP/UNP female genital/anal atlas:[/b] BakaUNP\VaginalAnalCanal2.dds plus _msn, _sk, and _s under the conventional female directory. These files target the matching vagina, anus, and canal geometries only.
[b]Argonian:[/b] BodySkin\YourSkinPack\Textures\actors\character\argonianfemale\... and argonianmale\...
[b]Khajiit:[/b] BodySkin\YourSkinPack\Textures\actors\character\khajiitfemale\... and khajiitmale\...
[b]UBE 2.0:[/b] BodySkin\YourSkinPack\Textures\!UBE\Body\femalebody_1_[d/n/sk].dds
BodySkin\YourSkinPack\Textures\!UBE\Head\femalehead_[d/n/sk].dds

Create one folder per skin pack and preserve the skin mod's original Textures tree and DDS files. One pack may contain all four Argonian/Khajiit race-sex folders; each populated combination is detected separately. Do not move UBE atlases into the conventional female folder. Catalog rows are matched to the selected actor's race, sex, and detected body family.

[size=4][color=#9AD7F5][b]Tint Packs[/b][/color][/size]
[b]TintMask\YourTintPack\textures\actors\character\character assets\tintmasks\*.dds[/b]

Create one folder per tint pack and preserve its RaceMenu tint-mask filenames and folder structure. Each folder directly under [b]TintMask[/b] becomes one entry in the in-game catalog.
For a UBE-only tint-mask pack, include [b]UBE[/b] in the top-level pack name. Packs marked [b]COtR[/b] are treated as compatible with both UBE and conventional female heads.

[b]Adding files while Skyrim is running[/b]

BodySlide preset XML files, skin-pack folders, and tint-pack folders may be added or replaced while the game is running. Open the corresponding [b]Body Presets[/b], [b]Body Skins[/b], or [b]Tint Masks[/b] tab and press [b]Refresh[/b] to rescan the files and update the list without restarting Skyrim.

The archive includes a README in every user-asset folder and a valid schema-4 distribution JSON with eight editable starter exclusions. Existing schema-3 files remain readable and are upgraded when saved.

[line]

[size=5][color=#5FB8E8][b]OPTIONAL OBODY NG JSON COMPATIBILITY[/b][/color][/size]

[b]This is optional.[/b] Body Change NG works without OBody NG or its JSON. Use this only if you want to reuse OBody NG-format distribution conditions, outfit-correction rules, or both.

[b]Optional OBody NG file[/b]
[b]Data\SKSE\Plugins\OBody_presetDistributionConfig.json[/b]

Place it beside [b]BodyChangeNGdistribution.json[/b] under [b]Data\SKSE\Plugins[/b]. Do not rename either file, merge the two JSON files, or replace Body Change NG's own JSON.

[list]
[*][b]Distribution conditions[/b] — press [b]Load saved values[/b] in the NPC Distribution window to import supported OBody distribution rules when the file exists
[*][b]Outfit-correction rules[/b] — press [b]Register OBody NG outfit-correction rules[/b] in the Outfit · randomization window
[*][b]Independent choices[/b] — import only distribution conditions, register only outfit-correction rules, or use both
[*][b]Read only[/b] — the OBody JSON is never read automatically at startup and is never modified by Body Change NG
[/list]

The [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/105052][b]OBody Next Generation ORefit JSON Master List[/b][/url] is a supported optional source. Its JSON and assets are not redistributed with Body Change NG.

[line]

[size=5][color=#5FB8E8][b]COMPATIBILITY NOTES[/b][/color][/size]

[list]
[*]Body Change NG does not edit NIFs, Skin Armor records, ArmorAddon records, or equipped slots
[*]Confirmed Body, Skin, and Tint selections are reapplied after RaceMenu closes
[/list]

